  "description": "Radicchio, a hearty bitter lettuce, becomes remarkably sweet and succulent when charred over a live fire. Served with a drizzle of good olive oil and saba—a sweet wine-based condiment—along with a sprinkle of gorgonzola cheese, it's the best vegetable you've never grilled.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: trevisano → radicchio; Saba syrup → balsamic syrup\n\nNotes: Saba or vincotto is a sweet syrup made from grape must. It's similar in flavor to a true Balsamic vinegar, though slightly less acidic. If you can't find it, any sort of balsamic condiment can be used in its place.",
